    "results": [
      {
        "obligationId": "scenario%3Aversion-owner-no-root-view::entry%3Adownload",
        "conclusion": "source_refuted",
        "explanation": "At the declared download entry, the source-visible path denies the request before any selected version file is served. The principal is the authenticated request.user; the entry dispatches download to file_response with attachment disposition. file_response binds the requested pk to request_doc, derives root_doc, and applies has_perms_owner_aware to root_doc—not to the caller-owned version. That check allows only an unowned root, the root owner, or a caller with the requested object permission. Under the supplied premise that another user owns the root and the caller has no object view grant, the check fails and returns HttpResponseForbidden. Consequently _get_effective_file_doc and serve_file are not reached for this scenario. If the gate were passed, the file object would be the effective file_doc selected from the requested root/version resolution, and serve_file would serve its archive_file or source_file; version ownership does not replace root authorization. No decisive source-external runtime fact is required within this declared boundary because the requested root binding, permission outcome, and existence are supplied as task premises, while the source path establishes the gate and protected effect. This is source_supported_failure, not a repository-wide completeness claim; source discovery remains not-tested.",
        "facts": {
          "entry": [
            {
              "statement": "DocumentViewSet.download dispatches the requested download to file_response with attachment disposition.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 1834,
                  "endLine": 1839,
                  "quote": "    @action(methods=[\"get\"], detail=True)\n    def download(self, request, pk=None):\n        try:\n            return self.file_response(pk, request, \"attachment\")\n        except (FileNotFoundError, Document.DoesNotExist):\n            raise Http404"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "binding": [
            {
              "statement": "The authorization check uses request.user as the caller identity when resolving the requested document.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 1401,
                  "endLine": 1427,
                  "quote": "    def _resolve_request_and_root_doc(\n        self,\n        pk,\n        request: Request,\n        *,\n        include_deleted: bool = False,\n    ) -> ResolvedRequestDocs | HttpResponseForbidden:\n        manager = Document.global_objects if include_deleted else Document.objects\n        try:\n            request_doc = manager.select_related(\n                \"owner\",\n                \"root_document\",\n            ).get(id=pk)\n        except Document.DoesNotExist:\n            raise Http404\n\n        root_doc = get_root_document(\n            request_doc,\n            include_deleted=include_deleted,\n        )\n        if request.user is not None and not has_perms_owner_aware(\n            request.user,\n            \"view_document\",\n            root_doc,\n        ):\n            return HttpResponseForbidden(\"Insufficient permissions\")\n        return ResolvedRequestDocs(request_doc=request_doc, root_doc=root_doc)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "The requested pk is bound to request_doc, and root_doc is derived from that requested document before authorization.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/views.py",
                  "startLine": 1410,
                  "endLine": 1420,
                  "quote": "            request_doc = manager.select_related(\n                \"owner\",\n                \"root_document\",\n            ).get(id=pk)\n        except Document.DoesNotExist:\n            raise Http404\n\n        root_doc = get_root_document(\n            request_doc,\n            include_deleted=include_deleted,\n        )"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "control": [
            {
              "statement": "The owner-aware check succeeds only when the object has no owner, the object owner is the user, or the object-level permission check succeeds.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "src/documents/permissions.py",
